IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Part I -- Preliminary. Ss 1 and 2 (short title, commencement) are machinery; s 2's date is `s2 day the Act came into operation` in the time module.
-- Section 3 (definitions) is in vic-definitions.l4.

§ `Part I -- Preliminary`

§§ `s 4 Application, construction and repeal provisions`

-- s 4(1)(a): the provisions extend and apply to all Acts and subordinate instruments, whether passed or made before or after the commencement, unless a contrary intention appears.
-- src:43 | (a) unless a contrary intention appears in this Act or in the Act or subordinate instrument concerned, extend and apply to all Acts, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Act, and to all subordinate instruments, whether made before or after that commencement; and
@ref s 4(1)(a) (src:43)
GIVEN kind IS A VicEnactmentKind, madeOrPassedOn IS A DATE, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s4(1)(a) the provisions of this Act extend and apply to the enactment` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 4(1)(b): the provisions apply to the interpretation of this Act.
-- The words "unless a contrary intention appears" are in paragraph (a) only, so this answer does not depend on the input; the input is kept so that (a) and (b) are called the same way.
-- src:44 | (b) apply to the interpretation of this Act.
@ref s 4(1)(b) (src:44)
GIVEN contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s4(1)(b) the provisions of this Act apply to the interpretation of this Act` MEANS
    JUST TRUE

-- s 4(2): nothing in this Act excludes a rule of construction applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with this Act.
-- src:45 | (2) Nothing in this Act excludes the application to an Act or subordinate instrument of a rule of construction applicable thereto and not inconsistent with this Act.
@ref s 4(2) (src:45)
GIVEN ruleApplicableToTheEnactment IS A BOOLEAN, ruleInconsistentWithThisAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s4(2) this Act leaves the rule of construction applying` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT ruleApplicableToTheEnactment THEN NOTHING
        IF ruleInconsistentWithThisAct THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 4(3): provisions expressed to apply to Acts passed or instruments made on or after the commencement do not affect the construction of an earlier Act or instrument, although it is continued in force or amended by a later one.
-- src:46 | (3) The provisions of this Act which are expressed to apply to Acts passed or subordinate instruments made on or after the commencement of this Act shall not affect the construction of any Act passed or subordinate instrument made before that commencement although that Act or subordinate instrument is continued in force or amended by an Act passed or subordinate instrument made on or after that commencement.
@ref s 4(3) (src:46)
GIVEN provisionExpressedToApplyOnlyFromCommencement IS A BOOLEAN, madeOrPassedOn IS A DATE, continuedOrAmendedByLaterEnactment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s4(3) the provision affects the construction of the enactment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT provisionExpressedToApplyOnlyFromCommencement THEN NOTHING
        IF madeOrPassedOn LESS THAN `s2 day the Act came into operation` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 5 Act to bind Crown`

DECLARE VicCapacityOfTheCrown IS ONE OF
    VicCrownInRightOfTheStateOfVictoria
    VicCrownInAnotherCapacity

-- s 5: binds the Crown in right of Victoria, and so far as the legislative power of the Parliament permits, the Crown in all its other capacities.
-- src:49 | 5 Act to bind Crown
-- src:50 | This Act binds the Crown, not only in right of the State of Victoria, but also, so far as the legislative power of the Parliament permits, the Crown in all its other capacities.
@ref s 5 (src:49-50)
GIVEN capacity IS A VicCapacityOfTheCrown, withinLegislativePowerOfTheParliament IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s5 this Act binds the Crown` MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN VicCrownInRightOfTheStateOfVictoria THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicCrownInAnotherCapacity THEN JUST withinLegislativePowerOfTheParliament
